From 5e04d690b1453a081cd838c404468af889c61ec0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirk Brown <kdborg@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 21:05:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Mersey: build the fork under the strict macOS toolchain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The macOS hermetic clang enforces gates the Linux-arm64 system-clang build
never did. Fix the fork's glue to compile and link cleanly:

- mersey_script_runner.h: ALLOW_DISCOURAGED_TYPE on the std::vector/std::map
  engine-boundary data members ([blink-style] find_bad_constructs plugin); mark
  MerseyScriptRunner `final` (-Wdelete-non-abstract-non-virtual-dtor: the cppgc
  finalizer calls the dtor on a class with virtuals).
- mersey_script_runner.cc: #pragma allow_unsafe_buffers — the C-ABI bridge's
  pointer/buffer arithmetic trips -Wunsafe-buffer-usage (whole-file opt-out for
  now; TODO: convert to spans).
- html_preload_scanner.cc: handle ScriptTypeAtPrepare::kMersey in the preload
  switch (-Werror,-Wswitch). Mersey scripts are inline-only — nothing to
  preload — so return false like the other inline types.
- third_party/mersey/BUILD.gn: link the engine as a cdylib on macOS, not a
  staticlib. A staticlib bundles a second copy of Rust's std and the link fails
  on `ld64: duplicate symbol: rust_eh_personality`; the cdylib exports only the
  msy_* C ABI and keeps its std internal (the same reason Linux uses the .so).
  libmersey_capi.dylib (install_name @rpath/…) is copied to the build root and
  resolved via an absolute rpath into it.

Built green: `autoninja chrome` on mac/arm64 (component release).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VfLS6F9bN1SzahLfBETDFe
